  <para style="h">Rud</para>
  <para style="toc1">Rud</para>
  <para style="toc2">Rud</para>
  <para style="toc3">Rud</para>
  <para style="mt1">Rud</para>
  <chapter number="1" style="c" sid="RUT 1" />
  <para style="s1">Ebe ye Nditọ Ideen Nọọmi Ekpañña</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="1" style="v" sid="RUT 1:1" />Ke idaha ini mme abiideikpe ekekarake, akañ amaaba ke isọñ. Ndin awodeen keed a-aketooho Betlehem ke Yuda, ye anwaan amọ ye nditọ ideen amọ iba emaekaiya adikidʌñ ke Mọb ke etək ini. <verse eid="RUT 1:1" /><verse number="2" style="v" sid="RUT 1:2" />Anyịñ awodeen ado akedo Elimelek, anyịñ anwaan amọ akedo Nọọmi, ñko nditọ ideen iba amọ ekekere Mahlọn ye Kiliọn. Ammọ ekedo mbon Efrad ke Betlehem, Yuda. Ndin ammọ emaekaa Mọb ekedʌñọ do.<verse eid="RUT 1:2" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="3" style="v" sid="RUT 1:3" />Akem ebe Nọọmi, Elimelek amaakpa, anye adinyʌñ asʌhọ ye nditọ ideen amọ iba. <verse eid="RUT 1:3" /><verse number="4" style="v" sid="RUT 1:4" />Ammọ emaedọi ibaan Mọb, keed akekere Ọpa, anye ako akekere Rud. Ke ammọ amaakedʌñ do ke ñkpọ nte isua duob, <verse eid="RUT 1:4" /><verse number="5" style="v" sid="RUT 1:5" />Mahlọn ye Kiliọn emaenyʌñ ekeene ekpañña, Nọọmi adiba ikpọọñ inieghe ayịn me ebe aba.<verse eid="RUT 1:5" /></para>
  <para style="s1">Nọọmi ye Rud Etịmme Enyọñ Betlehem</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="6" style="v" sid="RUT 1:6" />Ke ini Nọọmi aketieghe ke Mọb akop ke <char style="nd">Abọọñ</char> aditua mbon amọ mbọm ke adinọ ammọ ndidia, anye ye ibaan nditọ amọ emaebeeñe idem editịmme nto do ñnyọñ ufọk. <verse eid="RUT 1:6" /><verse number="7" style="v" sid="RUT 1:7" />Anye amaasaña ye ibaan nditọ amọ iba awuọ akpọñ itie anye akesidʌññọ anyʌñ adʌk usʌñ adiidat ammọ ñkewuọ abio Yuda.<verse eid="RUT 1:7" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="8" style="v" sid="RUT 1:8" />Ndin Nọọmi amaadọkkọ ibaan nditọ amọ awo iba ate, “Ndufo keedekeed, itịmme inyọñọ, ikaa ufọk eka ndufo. Yak <char style="nd">Abọọñ</char> iwọt ndufo mfọnido, kpa naña ndufo eñwọt miin ye mme akpañña ñkpa ebe ndufo mfọnido. <verse eid="RUT 1:8" /><verse number="9" style="v" sid="RUT 1:9" />Yak <char style="nd">Abọọñ</char> anam yak ndufo keedekeed enie mfọn ke iso ebe mfen ake ndufo ediidọ.”</para>
  <para style="p" vid="RUT 1:9">Ndin anye amaatʌm ammọ inua anyʌñ akọọm unyọñọ, ammọ emaenyʌñ etua ke akpọsọñ uyio <verse eid="RUT 1:9" /><verse number="10" style="v" sid="RUT 1:10" />ebo anye ete, “ñnyịn iyaukeene fiin inyọñ ikeene mbon ndufo.”<verse eid="RUT 1:10" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="11" style="v" sid="RUT 1:11" />Ado Nọọmi amaabo, “Nditọ mmi ibaan, itịmme inyọñ ufọk. Ntak a-ndufo eyemme iñkeene miin-e? Ado nte ami ñyaamaana mman nditọ ideen mfen se ikeme ediidọ ndufo? <verse eid="RUT 1:11" /><verse number="12" style="v" sid="RUT 1:12" />Nditọ mmi ibaan, itịmme inyọñ ufọk; Ami mmesọñ ñkan se ndọ ebe mfen. Akpekọm ami ñkpekere ke idodanyen asʌk aba annọ miin, akpekọm ñkpedọ ebe akonayio ami ñnyʌñ mmaan nditọ ideen, <verse eid="RUT 1:12" /><verse number="13" style="v" sid="RUT 1:13" />ndufo eyaebet yak ammọ ekpoon awo? Eyaetre udọ ndọ eda ebet ammọ? Iyoo nditọ ibaan mmi. Anekke adiọọk ye ami sia ubọk <char style="nd">Abọọñ</char> awọññọ añkpọñ miin!”<verse eid="RUT 1:13" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="14" style="v" sid="RUT 1:14" />Ke ntom ammọ emaana etua enweek. Ndin Ọpa amaatʌm ekaebe amọ inua akọọm anye unyọñ, ado Rud akpa ayịre anye.<verse eid="RUT 1:14" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="15" style="v" sid="RUT 1:15" />Nọọmi amaabo, “Sese, ke anwaan ndufo atịmme anyọñ abịne mbon amọ ye mme abasi amọ. Keene anye nyọñ.”<verse eid="RUT 1:15" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="16" style="v" sid="RUT 1:16" />Ado Rud amaabọọrọ anye ate, “Kuñkpek miin ubo ntịmme ukpọñ fiin me ñkanna iso ukpọñ fiin. Itie nte afo akaa ke ami ndiika, ñko nte afo aba ke ami ndiiba. Mbon mfo ediido mbon mmi ñko Abasi mfo ado Abasi mmi. <verse eid="RUT 1:16" /><verse number="17" style="v" sid="RUT 1:17" />Itie nte afo akpa ke ami ndiikpa, do ñko ke edimbuuk miin. Yak <char style="nd">Abọọñ</char> anam ye ami, kpa idiọọk-idiọọk, adieke ñkpa udiaññake fiin añkpọñ miin.” <verse eid="RUT 1:17" /><verse number="18" style="v" sid="RUT 1:18" />Nọọmi akekịt ke Rud amaabiide adikeene imọ, anye amaatre adikpak anye.<verse eid="RUT 1:18" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="19" style="v" sid="RUT 1:19" />Ke ntoro ibaan iba ado emaesaña keed tutu ekesịm Betlehem. Ke ammọ ekedisịmme Betlehem, afịd idʌñ ekpokko ke ntak ammọ, mme ibaan ebọñ ke ñkpaidem “Me Nọọmi akpedo ami?”<verse eid="RUT 1:19" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="20" style="v" sid="RUT 1:20" />Anye amaabo ammọ, “Ikiñkoot miin Nọọmi.<note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">1:20 </char><char style="ft" closed="false">Nọọmi awuọñọ adifọn</char></note>” Amaadian do, “Iñkoot miin Mara<note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">1:20 </char><char style="ft" closed="false">Mara awuọñọ idod</char></note> (ndod-ndod), sia Andikoñ Ñkan<note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">1:20 </char><char style="ft" closed="false">Ke usem Hibru ado Sadai; se ñko ke Rud 1:21</char></note> anam yak uwem mmi ado idod-idod. <verse eid="RUT 1:20" /><verse number="21" style="v" sid="RUT 1:21" />Ami ñkesaña ayọhọ ñwuọ, ado <char style="nd">Abọọñ</char> amben miin ñkaña anyọñ adi. Nsoo ido ntak eñkoodo miin Nọọmi? <char style="nd">Abọọñ</char> antʌhọde miin; Andikoñ Ñkan aben ndiọọkiso ansọk miin.”<verse eid="RUT 1:21" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="22" style="v" sid="RUT 1:22" />Ndin Nọọmi amaato Mọb anyọñ adi asaña ye Rud awonwaan Mọb, anwaan ayịn amọ, adiwuọ Betlehem ke ini idọk baali atọọñọke.<verse eid="RUT 1:22" /></para>
  <chapter eid="RUT 1" />
  <chapter number="2" style="c" sid="RUT 2" />
  <para style="s1">Rud Asoobo ye Boas ke Inwañ Ñkpasi</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="1" style="v" sid="RUT 2:1" />Ndin Nọọmi amaanie ayịnete ke edem ebe amọ, awuọiso awo ke ubon Elimelek, akereke Boas.<verse eid="RUT 2:1" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="2" style="v" sid="RUT 2:2" />Akem Rud awonwaan Mọb amaabo Nọọmi, “Yak ami ñka inwañ ñketañ ñyọhọnsʌhọ mfịd se eyaak ebono ke edem awo ndomokeed ake ami ndiikịt mfọn.”</para>
  <para style="p" vid="RUT 2:2">Nọọmi amaabo anye, “Ayịn mmi, kaa iso.” <verse eid="RUT 2:2" /><verse number="3" style="v" sid="RUT 2:3" />Ndin anye amaawuọ akedʌk inwañ atọọñọ adisara ñyọhọnsʌhọ mfịd ake mbon idọk emaekema utom. Akem anye amaakedʌk inwañ Boas, a-aketooho ubon Elimelek.<verse eid="RUT 2:3" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="4" style="v" sid="RUT 2:4" />Kpa idaha ado Boas amaato Betlehem adi adikọọm mme adọk idọk abo, “Yak <char style="nd">Abọọñ</char> aba ye ndufo!”</para>
  <para style="p" vid="RUT 2:4">Ammọ emaebọọrọ “<char style="nd">Abọọñ</char> udiọñ fiin.”<verse eid="RUT 2:4" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="5" style="v" sid="RUT 2:5" />Boas amaabịp aseñkpọ mbaña mbon idọk, “Anie inie ayịn abọikpa ako?”<verse eid="RUT 2:5" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="6" style="v" sid="RUT 2:6" />Adaiwuod ado amaabọọrọ, “Anye ado awonwaan Mọb a-akesañake ye Nọọmi ato adi. <verse eid="RUT 2:6" /><verse number="7" style="v" sid="RUT 2:7" />Anye amaabo, ‘Mbọk yak ami nsara mbeñe a-ayọhọke asʌhọ ke mme abek e-ebaaha ke edem mbon idọk.’ Anye amaadi inwañ adiba do tọọñọ ubakusen tutu idahami, ibọhọke etək nduọkadudu ke mfuud.”<verse eid="RUT 2:7" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="8" style="v" sid="RUT 2:8" />Ke ntoro Boas amaabo Rud, “Kpañ utọñ nnọ miin ayịn awonwaan. Kuukaa inwañ awo mfen ukusara, kuunyʌñ utịmme ukpọñ umi. Ba mi ye ibaan e-enamma utom ennọọ miin. <verse eid="RUT 2:8" /><verse number="9" style="v" sid="RUT 2:9" />Se naña mme ideen edọk idọk ke inwañ nyʌñ keene ibaan nam naña enam. Ami mmedọkkọ ideen mbo ke utuuk fiin ubọk. Ñko ini keed akeedodo itọñ usatta fiin, kaa kekoi mmọọñ ke abañ i-ideen emaekedọñ mmọọñ iyọhọ.”<verse eid="RUT 2:9" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="10" style="v" sid="RUT 2:10" />Ke ado anye amaanyuuk iwuod anyʌñ asuuk iso asịn ke isọñ. Anye amaabịp anye abo, “Ntaha ami nnieghe utọ mfọn ami ke iso mfo yak afo ammọọnọ miin asenawo?”<verse eid="RUT 2:10" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="11" style="v" sid="RUT 2:11" />Boas amaabọọrọ, “Endọkkọ miin ebaña afịd se afo anam anọọ ekaebe mfo tọọñọ ke ini ebe mfo akekpaaha naña afo akedakka akpọñ eka ye ete mfo ye isọñ emana mfo adidʌñ ye mbon awo afo umuudiọọñọke akpa. <verse eid="RUT 2:11" /><verse number="12" style="v" sid="RUT 2:12" />Yak <char style="nd">Abọọñ</char> unọ fiin utịb ke afịd se afo anam. Yak <char style="nd">Abọọñ</char> Abasi Isrel, a-afo adịbeke ke idak mba amọ anekke unọ fiin utịb.”<verse eid="RUT 2:12" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="13" style="v" sid="RUT 2:13" />Anye amaabo, “Abọọñ mmi, yak ami nsʌk ñkaiso nnie mfọn ke iso mfo.” Amaadian abo, “Afo amenam yak esịd antekke miin ana ke naña afo atañ ikọ ye ayịnufọk mfo, akpesʌkado ami mmendotto se ndo keed ke atu ayịnufọk mfo.”<verse eid="RUT 2:13" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="14" style="v" sid="RUT 2:14" />Ke ini ndidia, Boas amaabo anye, “Kanna di mmi. Di bọ uyo nyʌñ deep ke ukọd e-enamma ke fineka.”</para>
  <para style="p" vid="RUT 2:14">Ke ini anye asuuhọ atie ye mbon idọk, anye amaanọ anye ufọfọb ñkpasi. Anye amaadia ado ayʌkkọ anye amaana anie ñyọhọnsʌhọ. <verse eid="RUT 2:14" /><verse number="15" style="v" sid="RUT 2:15" />Ke anye adakkake ada adimaana nsara, Boas amaanọ ideen amọ uyio ate, “Yak anye akoono ke atu abek; ke awo ndomokeed aduat anye. <verse eid="RUT 2:15" /><verse number="16" style="v" sid="RUT 2:16" />Emekeme adisio ubaak ke atu mme abek idọk ebọppọ ebono, nọ anye yak adikoono, ñko ikiikpan anye.”<verse eid="RUT 2:16" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="17" style="v" sid="RUT 2:17" />Ke ntoro, Rud amaasara inwañ tutu ndubiayio. Ndin anye adomo baali se anye akesara ase ndin amaasịm ñkpọ nte udomoñkpọ efa<note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">2:17 </char><char style="ft" closed="false">Ñkpọ nte kilokram 13</char></note> keed. <verse eid="RUT 2:17" /><verse number="18" style="v" sid="RUT 2:18" />Anye amaaben anyọñ abio, ndin ekaebe amọ amaanyʌñ akekịt se anye aketañ. Rud amaanyʌñ asio se anye akedia asʌhọ ke anye amaakedia yak anekke ayʌkkọ anye, anọ anye.<verse eid="RUT 2:18" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="19" style="v" sid="RUT 2:19" />Ekaebe amọ amaabịp anye abo, “Ñke ke afo akesara mfịn? Ke mmọọ ke afo akenam utom? Afọfọn anọ awodeen u-ukịtte fiin!”</para>
  <para style="p" vid="RUT 2:19">Ndin Rud amaadọkkọ ekaebe amọ abaña awo anye akenamma utom ke itie amọ. Anye amaabo, “Anyịñ awo a-ami ñkenamma utom nnọ mfịn ado Boas.”<verse eid="RUT 2:19" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="20" style="v" sid="RUT 2:20" />Nọọmi abo anwaan ayịn amọ, “Yak <char style="nd">Abọọñ</char> adiọñ anye.” Abo, “Anye itreke adiwọt mme akpañkpa ye mme aduuwem mfọn amọ.” Anye amaadian do ate, “Ete ado, ado ataa ayịnete ñnyịn i-ikpereke ñnyịn idem; anye ado keed ke atu mme andifak isọñ a-ñnyịn inieghe.”<verse eid="RUT 2:20" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="21" style="v" sid="RUT 2:21" />Ndin Rud awonwaan Mọb amaabo, “Anye akap ambo miin, ‘Ba ye nditọufọk mmi tutu ammọ edọk idọk afịd ñkpasi mmi ema.’ ”<verse eid="RUT 2:21" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="22" style="v" sid="RUT 2:22" />Nọọmi amaabo Rud, anwaan ayịn amọ, “Ayịn mmi, akpaafọn afo adiba ye ibaan e-enamma utom enọ anye, sia ke inwañ awo mfen, e-ekeme adunọmọ fiin.”<verse eid="RUT 2:22" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="23" style="v" sid="RUT 2:23" />Rud amaaba akpere mme ibaan Boas anyʌñ asara ñkpọ tutu ammọ ekweeñe idọk baali ye idọk abakpa. Ndin anye amaadʌñ ye ekaebe amọ.<verse eid="RUT 2:23" /></para>
  <chapter eid="RUT 2" />
  <chapter number="3" style="c" sid="RUT 3" />
  <para style="s1">Rud ye Boas ke Isọñ Ukọkabakpa</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="1" style="v" sid="RUT 3:1" />Usen keed Nọọmi ekaebe Rud amaabo anye, “Ayịn awonwaan mmi, ana ami ñyem ufọk unọ fiin, itie se ediinekke ise ñkpọ ubaña fiin. <verse eid="RUT 3:1" /><verse number="2" style="v" sid="RUT 3:2" />Sese Boas, ake afo anamma utom ye mme ibaan amọ, ado ayịnete ñnyịn. Akonayio ami anye ayaakeñ mbio asio ke baali ke afe ubeek abakpa. <verse eid="RUT 3:2" /><verse number="3" style="v" sid="RUT 3:3" />Yie idem, fiọññọ pefium, ñnyʌñ sịne ataa uyaiya afọñ mfo. Ndin kaa afe ubeek abakpa, ado kuuyak anye adiọọñọ ke afo mmọdo aba do tutu anye adia ñkpọ anyʌñ anwọñ ukọd ama. <verse eid="RUT 3:3" /><verse number="4" style="v" sid="RUT 3:4" />Ke ini anye asuuhọ ana, diọọñọ itie a-anye anaaha. Ndin kaa ke fʌkkọ ukod amọ nyʌñ suuk naa. Anye ayaudọkkọ fiin se uduunam.”<verse eid="RUT 3:4" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="5" style="v" sid="RUT 3:5" />Rud amaabọọrọ, “Ami ñyaanam afịd se afo abo yak nnam.” <verse eid="RUT 3:5" /><verse number="6" style="v" sid="RUT 3:6" />Ndin anye amaadakka akaa afe ubeek abakpa akenam afịd se ekaebe amọ akebo anye anam.<verse eid="RUT 3:6" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="7" style="v" sid="RUT 3:7" />Ke ini Boas adiaha ñkpọ anyʌñ anwọñ ñkpọ ama, anye amaakaa akena ke akpatre utịd eboho mme mfịd. Rud amaadakka usʌk-usʌk akaa, akefʌkkọ anye ukod asuuk anaa. <verse eid="RUT 3:7" /><verse number="8" style="v" sid="RUT 3:8" />Ke ufọọd akonayio ñkpọ amaadịkke ete ado; anye akanna idem, ndin awonwaan mmọdo ana anye ke ukod!<verse eid="RUT 3:8" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="9" style="v" sid="RUT 3:9" />Anye amaabịp, “Afo ado anie?”</para>
  <para style="p" vid="RUT 3:9">Anye amaabọọrọ, “Ami ndo Rud ayịnufọk mfo.” Adian ndo, “Tat utọñ ewịra mfo mfʌk miin, sia afo adooho andifak anọọ mme mbon ekpək ñnyịn.”<verse eid="RUT 3:9" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="10" style="v" sid="RUT 3:10" />Anye amaabọọrọ, “Ayịn mmi awonwaan, <char style="nd">Abọọñ</char> udiọñ fiin. Mfọn anye ami a-akpon akan anye a-afo akeñwọttọ miin akpa ini koo: Afo ufegheke ukeene ntək ñkparawa, me e-enie akʌk me inieghe. <verse eid="RUT 3:10" /><verse number="11" style="v" sid="RUT 3:11" />Ndin idahami, ayịn mmi awonwaan, kuukop ndịk. Ami ñyaanam afịd se afo abeeñe unọ fiin. Afịd awo ke idʌñ ñnyịn e-ediọọñọ ke afo ado awonwaan a-anieghe eti edu. <verse eid="RUT 3:11" /><verse number="12" style="v" sid="RUT 3:12" />Akpesʌkado ado akpanikọ ke ami ndo andifak isọñ nnọọ ekpək ñnyịn, aba awo mfen anekkeke awuana ñkpọ añkan miin. <verse eid="RUT 3:12" /><verse number="13" style="v" sid="RUT 3:13" />Ba mi akonayio ami tutu ubakusen, adieke anye ayemme adinam utom amọ nte andufak a-aseeghe ñkpọ ubaña, a-afọn; yak anye ufak fiin. Ado adieke anye imiimaaha, adaña nte <char style="nd">Abọọñ</char> aduuho uwem ami ñyaanam. Naa mmi tutu ayio asiere.”<verse eid="RUT 3:13" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="14" style="v" sid="RUT 3:14" />Ndin anye amaanaa ke ukod amọ tutu ayio asiere, ado amaabak ademme mbemiso awo adiọọñọ; anye amaanyʌñ abo, “Inaaha awo ndomokeed adiọọñọ ke awonwaan amaadi afe ubeek abakpa.”<verse eid="RUT 3:14" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="15" style="v" sid="RUT 3:15" />Anye amaamaana abo, “Ben adifʌhọ afọñ a-afo asịneke do di dette nnọ.” Ke ini anye akenamma ntoro, anye amaanwañña mfịd baali ñkpọ nte udomo itiokeed adọñ anọ anye anyʌñ adịppe anọ anye. Ndin anye Boas atịmme anyọñ abio.<verse eid="RUT 3:15" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="16" style="v" sid="RUT 3:16" />Ke ini Rud akekaaha abịne ekaebe amọ, Nọọmi amaabịp anye, “Ayịn awonwaan mmi akeba die?”</para>
  <para style="p" vid="RUT 3:16">Ndin anye amaadọkkọ anye afịd se Boas akenam anọ anye <verse eid="RUT 3:16" /><verse number="17" style="v" sid="RUT 3:17" />anyʌñ adian do, “Anye amannọ miin udomo baali itiokeed abo, ‘Kuunyọñ ubịne ekaebe mfo ubọk-ubọk.’ ”<verse eid="RUT 3:17" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="18" style="v" sid="RUT 3:18" />Ndin Nọọmi amaabo, “Ayịn awonwaan mmi, bet, tutu afo adiọọñọ se itịppe. Sia ete ado idiiduọkkọ adudu tutu anye adiọọñọ iwuod ñkpọ ado mfịn.”<verse eid="RUT 3:18" /></para>
  <chapter eid="RUT 3" />
  <chapter number="4" style="c" sid="RUT 4" />
  <para style="s1">Boas Adọ Rud</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="1" style="v" sid="RUT 4:1" />Akem Boas amaadọọk akaa inuaatob abio akesuuk atie do nte andifakka isọñ ake anye aketañña abaña adiisaña adiboiyo. Boas amaabo, “Ufan mmi, saña di umi, di suuk tie mi.” Ndin anye amaasaña akesuuk atie.<verse eid="RUT 4:1" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="2" style="v" sid="RUT 4:2" />Boas amaaben mme ñkpisọñ duob ke abio anyʌñ abo, “Isuuk itie mi,” ammọ emaenyʌñ enam ntoro. <verse eid="RUT 4:2" /><verse number="3" style="v" sid="RUT 4:3" />Ndin anye amaabo andifakka isọñ ado, “Nọọmi, a-aketooho abio Mọb anyọñ adi a-anyam isọñ a-ayịnete ñnyịn Elimelek akenieghe. <verse eid="RUT 4:3" /><verse number="4" style="v" sid="RUT 4:4" />Ami mmaakere ke akpena nnam yak afo adiọọñọ ñkpọ ami ñnyʌñ mbo yak afo adep ke iso mbon e-etieghe mi ye ke iso mme ñkpisọñ mmi ami. Akpedo afo ayaafakka anye, nam ntoro. Ado akpedo afo umuuduunamma, ndọkkọ miin nọ ami ndiọọñọ. Sia ibaaha awo ndomokeed mfen se inie unen adinam ami imiibọhọke afo, ñko ami ukeene fiin ke edem.”</para>
  <para style="p" vid="RUT 4:4">Anye amaabo, “Ami ñyaafakka anye.”<verse eid="RUT 4:4" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="5" style="v" sid="RUT 4:5" />Ndin Boas amaatañ abo, “Usen ake afo adep isọñ ado ato Nọọmi, afo anyʌñ adep Rud awonwaan Mọb, ebekpa ayịn ado, nọ ato do anyịñ akpañkpa asʌk aba ye inie amọ.”<verse eid="RUT 4:5" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="6" style="v" sid="RUT 4:6" />Ke ami, andifakka isọñ amaabo, “Akpedo ntoro ami ndiikanna mfakka sia akeme adibiat inie mmi. Afo kappa fakka ke idem mfo. Ami ndiikanna nnam.”<verse eid="RUT 4:6" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="7" style="v" sid="RUT 4:7" />(Ndin naña akesido ke ido Isrel, ke adifakka ye adiyaak nnọ adinie nsọọñọnda, ana awo keed asio ikpaukod amọ anọ awo anye ako. Ntom ke ekesidat esọọñọ utọ adinam ami ke Isrel.)<verse eid="RUT 4:7" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="8" style="v" sid="RUT 4:8" />Ke ntoro andifak isọñ ado amaabo Boas, “Ben dep ke idem mfo.” Ndin anye amaasio ikpaukod amọ.<verse eid="RUT 4:8" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="9" style="v" sid="RUT 4:9" />Ndin Boas amaabo mme ñkpisọñ ye afịd awo, “Mfịn ami ndufo emedo ntiense ke ami mmedep afịd inie Elimelek, Kiliọn ye Mahlọn nto Nọọmi. <verse eid="RUT 4:9" /><verse number="10" style="v" sid="RUT 4:10" />Ami mmenyʌñ ndep Rud awo Mọb, ebekpa Mahlọn, nte anwaan mmi, nọ ato do ami nsʌk ñkaiso nnịm anyịñ akpañkpa ye mme inie amọ, mbaak anyịñ amọ adisop ke atu ekpək amọ me ke abio idʌñ amọ. Mfịn ndufo emedo ntiense!”<verse eid="RUT 4:10" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="11" style="v" sid="RUT 4:11" />Ndin afịd mme ñkpisọñ ye afịd awo se ikiba ke inuaatob emaebo, “Ñnyịn ido mme ntiense. Yak <char style="nd">Abọọñ</char> anam awonwaan a-adʌkkọ adi ufọk mfo aba nte Ratiel ye Lia, e-ekedaaha keed ebọp ekpək Isrel. Afo akpekap anie idaha ke Efrata anyʌñ awuọ etob ke Betlehem. <verse eid="RUT 4:11" /><verse number="12" style="v" sid="RUT 4:12" />Ato ke nditọ <char style="nd">Abọọñ</char> unọọhọ fiin ato abọikpa awonwaan ami, yak ubon mfo aba nte ubon Peres, ake Tama akemanna anọ Yuda.”<verse eid="RUT 4:12" /></para>
  <para style="s1">Nọọmi Anie Udod Ayịn Awodeen</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="13" style="v" sid="RUT 4:13" />Ndin Boas amaaben Rud anye adido anwaan amọ. Ke ini anye akenamma ima ye anye, <char style="nd">Abọọñ</char> amaanam anye ayommo idịb, anye amaanyʌñ aman ayịn. <verse eid="RUT 4:13" /><verse number="14" style="v" sid="RUT 4:14" />Ibaan emaebo Nọọmi: “Itooro anie <char style="nd">Abọọñ</char> i-imiiyakka afo anana andifakka isọñ ke usen ami. Yak anye adiiwuọ etob ke afịd Isrel! <verse eid="RUT 4:14" /><verse number="15" style="v" sid="RUT 4:15" />Anye ayaademme uwem mfo anyʌñ ukama fiin ke ini usọñ mfo. Sia anwaan ayịn mfo, u-umaaha fiin eti-eti a-anyʌññọ afọn ye afo akan nditọ ideen itiaba, ado andiman anye.”<verse eid="RUT 4:15" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="16" style="v" sid="RUT 4:16" />Ndin Nọọmi amaaben ayịn ado akama ke ubọk amọ anyʌñ ado adep anọ anye. <verse eid="RUT 4:16" /><verse number="17" style="v" sid="RUT 4:17" />Mme ibaan e-ekedʌññọ do emaebo, “Nọọmi anie ayịn!” Ammọ enyʌñ esio anye anyịñ Obed. Anye akedo ete Yesi, a-akedooho ete Defid.<verse eid="RUT 4:17" /></para>
  <para style="s1">Ubon Defid</para>
  <para style="li4">
    <verse number="18" style="v" sid="RUT 4:18" />Ami ndin ado ubon Peres:</para>
  <para style="b" vid="RUT 4:18" />
  <para style="li1" vid="RUT 4:18">Peres akedo ete Hesrọn,<verse eid="RUT 4:18" /></para>
  <para style="li1">
    <verse number="19" style="v" sid="RUT 4:19" />Hesrọn ado ete Ram,</para>
  <para style="li1" vid="RUT 4:19">Ram abon Aminadab,<verse eid="RUT 4:19" /></para>
  <para style="li1">
    <verse number="20" style="v" sid="RUT 4:20" />Aminadab ado ete Nasọn,</para>
  <para style="li1" vid="RUT 4:20">Nasọn abon Salmọn,<verse eid="RUT 4:20" /></para>
  <para style="li1">
    <verse number="21" style="v" sid="RUT 4:21" />Salmọn abon Boas,</para>
  <para style="li1" vid="RUT 4:21">Boas abon Obed,<verse eid="RUT 4:21" /></para>
  <para style="li1">
    <verse number="22" style="v" sid="RUT 4:22" />Obed ado ete anọ Yesi,</para>
  <para style="li1" vid="RUT 4:22">ndin Yesi abon Defid.<verse eid="RUT 4:22" /></para>
  <chapter eid="RUT 4" />
</usx>